two-stage estimation procedure\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Crash rates are calculated by dividing the number of alcohol-involved crashes for each age group by the census estimate\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"This model produces estimates that are not comparable to those produced by the imputation procedure used by FARS before 2002\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\", \"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}